'' WHAT A SAME-SIZE POINTER 'operator cast' DOES NOT REACH (structpick.tiko PtrCastScore). In an
'' overload set, the pointee ranked FIRST in the parameter's row scores back exactly HALF, which
'' fbc's hCheckCastOvlEx turns into no match: 'ubyte ptr' into 'zstring ptr', 'ushort ptr' into
'' 'wstring ptr' -- fbc's 99, where tiko stopped on TKO0994. Another size and derived-to-base are
'' 58 (a single procedure); two casts at the best score are 98 -- 'zstring ptr' and 'any ptr' into
'' 'ubyte ptr', 'zstring ptr' and 'ubyte ptr' into 'byte ptr'. The same 'ubyte ptr' cast into a
'' single 'byte ptr' procedure binds (line 58), where tiko said TKO0698. Lines identical to
'' fbc-modern's errors. Line 79: an exact pointee scores the same const or not, so 'byte ptr' and
'' 'const zstring ptr' casts tie two overloads (98). Lines 93-94: a 'zstring ptr' cast that fbc picks
'' for a 'string' parameter is a bottom-tier match in a set -- tied with 'byte ptr' (98), alone the
'' 58. Line 103: an assignment dropping the picked cast's pointee const (181); line 102 is fine.
'' Line 111: one 'zstring ptr' cast, the same two overloads -- a tie, where the call was untyped.
